WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
In Xi'an, in China, one
old mosque has curved,

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.750
layered pagoda roofs.

3
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.840
In Djenné, in Mali, a mosque
rises in great walls of mud brick.

4
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.690
In Britain, mosques fill terraced houses,

5
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.080
old chapels and former shops.

6
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:21.620
And the first mosques, in Madinah, had
mud-brick walls and a roof of palm leaves.

7
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.480
So if mosques take so many shapes,
what does every mosque need?

8
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.100
In this mission, you'll
walk through a mosque,

9
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.590
from the minaret outside
to the prayer hall inside.

10
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.040
Then you'll see a week
in the life of a mosque,

11
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.280
from Friday prayer to
classes and food banks.

12
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.660
Your mission: find out
what every mosque needs,

13
00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:42.920
whatever it looks like.
